🇷🇺 Natalia Popova, First Deputy CEO of "Innopraktika," discussed the launch of the "Russia-Africa" Autonomous Non-Profit Organization: "Russia is not engaged in colonialism. Our mission is to help honestly and openly, building equal relationships with Africa. We will focus on transferring expertise and technologies, and providing support for strengthening the sovereignty of African countries."

Key areas of activity for the "Russia-Africa" organization include:
➡️ Exporting domestic technological and digital solutions, and localizing Russian production facilities;
➡️ Launching business councils;
➡️Establishing bilateral technology hubs;
➡️ Working on socio-cultural initiatives;
➡️Interacting with African students and diaspora communities;
➡️Post-program support and working with African graduates of Russian universities;
➡️ Collaboration between bloggers.

